attacked vehicles carrying European diplomats in the West Bank, a day after an American photographer was beaten. Belgium and France have condemned the attack.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How big is Russia's threat against Germany?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:662b32d8ba39f834f0bb4c5637c746b96988aaeb1cd6b41a4397d7ee76695f3a</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T15:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426--e8db9669a70a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-big-is-russia-s-threat-against-germany/a-79688426?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts believe that, so far, Germany has been ill-prepared — both militarily and mentally — for Russian provocations. They also warn against the idea that ending support for Ukraine would make Germany safer.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>China's influence in the gaming industry is growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dde3abb0b99299d2b1d2a9387714d3581718379939af01081fa8b67aa7bc3b65</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755--447380e7608a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-influence-in-the-gaming-industry-is-growing/a-79484755?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home to more than 700 million gamers, China is the world's largest gaming market — but it's also one of the most tightly regulated. The effects reach far beyond China, impacting players around the world.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo leaves hospital after cancer surgery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7f6c4b63a7875d310aa64e20184cd38de47c45773ab47774ea44ad651d6da198</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-leaves-hospital-after-cancer-surgery/a-79688162--69f6144ccc39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pope-leo-leaves-hospital-after-cancer-surgery/a-79688162?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Four days after undergoing surgery for lung cancer, Pope Leo left the hospital in Rome. His doctors said he was well enough to return home.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia wants blackout in Ukraine as winter comes — Zelenskyy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9837fddcec3480be92e0ee267a42eee6a05d4cefeefc79fc1b9aa32c63841c1a</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T11:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703--c66cb23b1a91.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Zelenskyy says Russia is trying to cut electricity and heating to civilians ahead of winter. He also called the US president's waiver of new sanctions on Moscow a boost for Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Berlin's leftist parties move step closer to forming government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d278e5905033946203284054b5fc72acb413fcdd4e3888c85374d4de9a547b69</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:48:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-s-leftist-parties-move-step-closer-to-forming-government/live-79686913--8bbbc4d4b09d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-berlin-s-leftist-parties-move-step-closer-to-forming-government/live-79686913?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Berlin's left-leaning parties have successfully concluded exploratory talks, and formal coalition negotiations could begin next month if party members approve. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Mexico sentences killers of US, Australian surfers to 158 years each in prison</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:854c9c05a8e0a321ab5a6ec3c429905b2959848e189253b3e4c7a524b6addc42</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/mexico-sentences-killers-of-us-australian-surfers-to-158-years-each-in-prison/a-79685975--d9f256fde01a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/mexico-sentences-killers-of-us-australian-surfers-to-158-years-each-in-prison/a-79685975?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three Mexican men were found guilty last week of murdering foreign surfers in 2024. The case had drawn global condemnation, particularly in Australia, where two of the victims were from.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Protesters clash with police in nationwide protests, amid rising social polarization</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4e63a6dd397081688b0848dec144dce02d807f619c1cbc6b873d8b9a3503907</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:48:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T08:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584--b410e6f9b726.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-protesters-clash-with-police-in-nationwide-protests-amid-rising-social-polarization/a-79685584?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Unrest broke out in parts of France as students, trade unionists and Yellow Vest activists took to the streets to protest high prices and inequality. Police arrested over 1,000 people amid chaotic scenes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: California wildfires destroy homes, leave thousands without power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed2dc29f67bbbe31605dca5174b3620f1a1e636ec194f0f38346babcc673163a</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T06:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-california-wildfires-destroy-homes-leave-thousands-without-power/a-79685480--49bdc655ff84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-california-wildfires-destroy-homes-leave-thousands-without-power/a-79685480?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Multiple mansions have been engulfed in the fires raging in California while firefighters continue to douse the blaze. Thousands of people have been evacuated and many others are without power.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Oregon school shooting: Police praise 'heroism' of those who intervened to stop more killing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f343ece869ce223d16c8c34be2e20e63fc0c6ded08a0ec3379f5a494b238628b</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T06:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-police-praise-heroism-of-those-who-intervened-to-stop-more-killing/a-79685302--68385910c32e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/oregon-school-shooting-police-praise-heroism-of-those-who-intervened-to-stop-more-killing/a-79685302?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US police have praised the actions of three people who cut short a deadly shooting at a school in the state of Oregon. Three children and a teacher were killed in the attack, carried out by a former pupil at the school.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump puts new Russia sanctions on hold</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b76fa5c8b51955bcc2b6fad54074322c0f6ebd87e7b11ee5dd03a91871d0e87d</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-17T02:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-puts-new-russia-sanctions-on-hold/a-79685002--586e2562981b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-puts-new-russia-sanctions-on-hold/a-79685002?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US president cited national interests for his decision to sign a waiver on sanctions Congress voted to place on Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Amazon deforestation lowest in nearly 40 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed73a1a16200ec2c642a86c8396f1d589b66edfd646da89f5ba81267e9557465</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T22:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-amazon-deforestation-lowest-in-nearly-40-years/a-79684906--24b7e4d329ee.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-amazon-deforestation-lowest-in-nearly-40-years/a-79684906?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The latest figures show that 3,335 square kilometers of the Amazon rainforest were cleared in the year ending in July, the lowest level since 1988. The drop has been described as an "historic achievement."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukrainian President Zelenskyy speaks at EU summit amid spat with Donald Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:284763a133c1d543cb26c45f8ae5ca94c3352fa931c3ca0e42982c4d6921fada</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340--6307cb90b3ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukrainian-president-zelenskyy-speaks-at-eu-summit-amid-spat-with-donald-trump/a-79684340?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU leaders reaffirmed support for Ukraine at the Brussels summit. But souring relations with the US over Russia and Starlink and a big hole in the budget will make for a difficult winter for Ukraine.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>West Bank: US journalist injured by Israeli settlers</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d0a4f18f18d3860db9082beac93631663b9292d112fd5ba790403d923a6edb4</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/west-bank-us-journalist-injured-by-israeli-settlers/a-79684181--8e9b6bd6853f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/west-bank-us-journalist-injured-by-israeli-settlers/a-79684181?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Washington Post journalist Heidi Levine said she was beaten by Israeli settlers in the occupied West Bank. Reporters Without Borders slammed the attack as "brazen violence."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>White House press secretary Zacharia exiting role after short tenure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6b5ca4b0140518e82b53a03d61f5593e8a510e17b9089769eb724e64b6839eb</id><updated>2026-10-18T04:47:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-16T19:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-exiting-role-after-short-tenure/a-79684341--2f88277a7fd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/white-house-press-secretary-zacharia-exiting-role-after-short-tenure/a-79684341?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Zacharia, having served only five days in the role, is now the shortest-serving press secretary in White House history. Her departure follows a rocky debut at the podium and controversy surrounding her background.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
